description:
Decode and build the `lParam` of `WM_KEYDOWN` and `WM_KEYUP` (lesson 2.01's table), and name virtual keys:

```cpp
using LPARAM = std::int64_t;
struct KeyInfo { int repeat; int scanCode; bool extended; bool altDown; bool wasDown; bool released; };

KeyInfo decodeKey(LPARAM lParam);
LPARAM encodeKey(const KeyInfo& k);
bool isFirstPress(LPARAM lParam);      // a key-down that is not an auto-repeat
std::string keyName(int vk);
```

`keyName`: `'A'`-`'Z'` and `'0'`-`'9'` are themselves; `0x70`-`0x87` are `F1`-`F24`; `0x08` Backspace, `0x09` Tab, `0x0D` Enter, `0x1B` Esc, `0x20` Space, `0x21` PageUp, `0x22` PageDown, `0x23` End, `0x24` Home, `0x25` Left, `0x26` Up, `0x27` Right, `0x28` Down, `0x2D` Insert, `0x2E` Delete; anything else `"0x"` and two upper-case hex digits (such as `0xBA`).

